{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable fits my television and DVD-player purchases because it could help connect equipment I already use, and the longer cable could help with placement.",
    "The SanDisk memory card fits my repeated purchases of removable storage, adapters, and a card reader, although I would need to confirm support for 256GB microSDXC."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo devices and portable speaker introduce uses I have not shown a need for; my purchases mostly help me connect, maintain, or equip existing devices.",
    "The Lightning earbuds do not follow from my 30-pin cable purchase because the connector matters. Likewise, owning a Fire tablet does not mean I currently want an iPad replacement.",
    "Having a television makes the HDMI cable useful, but it does not by itself give me a reason to add a streaming device."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been treated as interest in almost any electronic device, even when it serves an unrelated purpose.",
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been stretched into interest in more Amazon devices, although their functions differ from the accessories I keep buying."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly buy practical supporting items such as cables, mounts, memory-card holders, power strips, and camera accessories, so the job an item solves matters more than a shared brand.",
    "Compatibility details matter: connector type, memory-card format and capacity support, and camera fit determine whether an otherwise relevant accessory is usable.",
    "My latest lens-cap purchase and earlier tripods suggest continued attention to camera equipment, which these recommendations barely address."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my storage and connection needs but read my electronics purchases too broadly as a desire for additional devices."
}"}
